cff-version: 1.2.0
title: Orebit Synthetic Drillhole Datasets
message: >-
  If you use these datasets, please cite them as below.
type: dataset
authors:
  - given-names: Ghozian Islam
    family-names: Karami
    affiliation: Orebit.id
repository-code: 'https://github.com/ghoziankarami/orebit-datasets'
abstract: >-
  Three fully synthetic drillhole datasets covering the deposit
  styles most relevant to Indonesian mineral exploration:
  low-sulphidation epithermal gold, nickel laterite, and alluvial
  tin placer. Generated from geological models rather than
  collected from any real deposit, so they carry no third-party
  rights and can be redistributed, taught from, and bundled into
  software without a licence review. Each dataset uses an
  identical four-file layout (collar, survey, assay, litho) but a
  deliberately different statistical character, making the set
  useful for testing whether one workflow generalises across
  deposit styles.
keywords:
  - drillhole data
  - resource estimation
  - geostatistics
  - synthetic dataset
  - epithermal gold
  - nickel laterite
  - alluvial tin
  - Indonesia
  - open data
license: CC-BY-4.0
version: 1.0.0
date-released: '2026-08-29'
